<title>JAPAN: Japan scraps another restriction on forex payments.</title>
<headline>Japan scraps another restriction on forex payments.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) said on Monday that it had abolished restrictions on currency transactions for export and import payments with a gap of more than two years between the shipment of goods and the settlement.</p>
<p>The measure took effect on September 1, a MOF official said. Previously, firms were required to get approval from the ministry for such foreign exchange transactions.</p>
<p>The move is part of the ministry's deregulatory measures announced in March and June. The ministry will try to put the remaining steps in place as soon as possible, the official added.</p>
</text>
